remakes and remasters aren't always my  favorite thing given there's the concern  that it's taking time away from  developers making new games that said  this certainly old games where it's  lovely to see them get a new lick of  paint here are four of those such games  that we can expect this year gamers were  a little burned by the fact that Final  Fantasy 7 / ps4 announced during the  PlayStation experience wasn't a noob  remaster but rather a port of the PC  version nonetheless there is a future  where you can play one of the best Final  Fantasy games on your ps4 so it's not  all bad the graphics have been upscaled  from their original 1997 resolution but  it's still largely blocky polygons  galore if you can put up with that and  you still have a truckload of nostalgic  love for the JRPG it could be worth  picking up the port from the PC version  also accumulates all the fixes from over  the years and features a character  booster which drastically boosts the  skill of a party on a save file so the  player can experience the story and not  need to grind for levels take this entry  with a grain of salt but since gamers  haven't been waiting for some kind of  Final Fantasy 7 remaster since the  possibility was first teased in 2005  this is at least a start speaking of the  best entries in long-running series  another game that came out in the late  90s is getting the remastered treatment  this month with Heroes of Might and  Magic 3 HD although it's nowhere near as  much of an upgrade as Ubisoft tried to  convince us it was since you wouldn't  really define the retouched up character  sprites as HD it's still a step up with  the game support for modern resolutions  there's also the addition of a  multiplayer Lobby compatible with steam  works to make playing online a whole lot  easier  unfortunately the excellent expansions  aren't included as a result of lost  source code the latest entry Heroes of  Might and Magic 6 might be detailed and  colorful but Heroes 3 had the best  strategy and town building elements of  this series which they've had trouble  topping ever since  this month isn't short of great  remasters since we're also hours away  from getting our hands on the new and  improved grim fandago the critically  acclaimed 1998 game from Tim Schafer is  considered a classic in the history of  adventure games but as is the case with  most 90s games getting it running on  modern machines is no small task and the  game's clunky Resident Evil style tank  controls were never a popular feature as  a result Double Fine has taken on the  task of producing a remaster for the ps4  Vita PC Mac and Linux platforms and  they're determined to do it right they  got in contact with players who had  written unofficial patches in some cases  requesting their code to integrate into  the remaster Similac who was also  involved they relied on uncovering 130  discs worth of original game assets  LucasArts had in their archives so they  didn't have to work with compressed art  thanks to that the game is set to  feature high res textures and character  models real-time lighting and the  ability to switch between the original  and the remastered graphics there's an  optional new control scheme and a  developer's commentary track for the  hardcore fans and the remake of remaster  I'm most excited for this year is the  Legend of Zelda Majora's Mask 3d if like  me you find yourself with the childhood  around the 90s and happened to have a  3ds this wonderfully moody entry into  the Legend of Zelda series offers a  delightfully dark world to explore like  al Carina of time 3d majora's mask 3d  will take advantage of the 3d s's  touchscreen controls gyroscope and  obviously 3d visuals as well as  incorporating better textures and  lighting the gameplay is also going to  be quote smoother according to creator  Aegean Numa and there will be changes  like altered boss battles and the  addition of fishing fans of the series  spent four years campaigning for this  remake ever since Ocarina of Time 3d was  released back in 2011 are you a fan of  remakes let me know which one of these  titles you're keen to play this year  a whole other game you want to get your  hands on I will see you next week
 

